course: dictionary
lesson: 10854
title: The power to say no
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A veto is the power to say no and stop a decision or law, even when everyone else agrees with it. «Mum vetoed the idea of a puppy» means Mum said no, so there is no puppy. You can test it: swap in «said no and stopped» and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Veto is also a verb. You can veto, he vetoes, she vetoed, they are vetoing. In the UN Security Council, each of the five permanent members can veto a decision on its own, so one «no» can block the whole decision.
explain: At school or home you can use the word in a lighter way. If your friends want to go to the cinema and you refuse, you have vetoed the idea. The clues are «refuse» and «no», so veto means to refuse something firmly.
fact: Veto is a noun (a veto) and a verb (to veto).
fact: A veto is the right to stop a decision or law, even if others agree with it.
fact: The US President can veto a bill passed by Congress.
fact: Congress can override a veto if two-thirds of both the House and the Senate vote for the bill again.
fact: The five permanent members of the UN Security Council are the USA, Russia, China, the UK and France.
exercise: «Mum vetoed the idea of a puppy.» What does vetoed mean here? | Said yes and bought a puppy | Forgot all about the idea | *Said no and stopped it | Asked the vet for help
exercise: «Each permanent member of the UN Security Council can veto a decision.» What power does a veto give? | The power to vote twice | The power to speak first | *The power to block a decision with one no | The power to stop a decision
exercise: Which word means to say no and stop a decision? | permanent | *veto | decision | bill
test: «The bill was vetoed by the President.» Who stopped the bill? | *The President | The children | The UN | Congress
test: «Congress can override a veto if two-thirds vote again.» What does override suggest? | Accept the veto without a fight | *Win against the veto and make the bill law | Write a poem about the bill | Forget the bill
exam: «Think of a school council: five pupils who can veto any plan.» What does veto mean in this sentence? | Vote for the plan twice | Write down the plan | Say yes to every plan | *Say no and stop the plan
